     {
      "id": "ryland-maxwell-trade",
      "kind": "trade",
      "headline": "One Star Out, Three In, and the Smallest Piece Was the Prize",
      "body": [
       "When Skura left New York for Atlanta after Y82, the deal that went with him looked lopsided, just not the way it turned out. Malakai Sawyer went back to the Jets as an 89-rated back with a B grade, 203 games and 13,041 career rushing yards, his card priced at 1,755. Coming the other way were Maxwell, rated 65 and valued at 12, Chance Woodrum, a 74-rated defensive back valued at 70, and Kane Van Oxley, \"The Ox\", an S-grade receiver valued at 1,515.",
       "Was it a risk? By the numbers that winter, Sawyer's card was worth more than a hundred times Maxwell's, and the best asset Atlanta received never played for it: in an offseason of three- and four-team trades across the league, Van Oxley was moved on to the Bears before a single Falcons game. The bet came down to Maxwell and Woodrum. Sawyer played 96 more games and won no more rings. Woodrum won 5 more. Maxwell won 11."
      ],
