      "kind": "market",
      "headline": "From 7 to 49,485, a Season Late Every Time",
      "body": [
       "The card told the story a season late every time. It was worth 7 at the end of Y80 and 12 on the day of the trade. It reached 112 after Y84, with two Falcons titles already won, and 1,520 after Y86. It first passed Sawyer's in Y88, at 7,837, and more than doubled in Y92 alone, from 12,722 to 29,409, the season he ran for 2,839 yards. After Y94 it stood at 39,532, and it closed at 49,485 after Y96, his last season."
