     {
      "id": "ryland-maxwell-last-lap",
      "kind": "lastlap",
      "headline": "Two More Rings, First All Time, and a First-Ballot Hall of Famer",
      "body": [
       "There was no argument left to settle, and he played on anyway. In Y95 he ran for 2,141 yards and won a 12th ring, playing 18 of the Eagles' 20 games after injury cost him 2, and passed Sherman Brandson for first in Career Legacy, 14,019 to 13,540. Y96, at 34, was the last: 2,574 yards and 25 rushing touchdowns in 21 games, a 13th ring after a 40-26 win over the Bengals, and a 7th Super Bowl MVP. Then he retired, with the career rushing record at 32,108 yards, and the Hall of Fame took him at once, on the first ballot, in the Class of Y96, with a score of 99."
      ],
